msgid "802.11k neighbor report"
msgstr ""

msgid "802.11k/v/r only publish information: an AP can answer \"who else is there\", and a client can ask on its own. DAWN does the other half — it aggregates what every device sees for each client, scores the candidate APs, and then has the current AP hand the client to a better one with a BSS Transition. With two devices on the same SSID and nothing making that decision, a client sticks to its original AP until the signal dies completely."
