msgid "The two buttons above act on all SSIDs at once; the toggles in the table only change the interface on that row. The MD column is editable: enter 4 hex digits (0-9 / a-f), or clear it to fall back to the SSID-derived value. Editing one interface updates every interface of the same SSID, otherwise FT will not work when roaming across bands. Enable it, then use \"Wired sync\" to push the config to the other devices so the whole group shares the same SSID and MD."
msgstr ""

msgid "The whole network as DAWN sees it: which APs broadcast the same SSID, who is connected to each AP, and how loudly each client is heard by the other APs. Use it to tell whether roaming is actually working — instead of guessing."
msgstr ""

msgid "There are no AP interfaces."
msgstr ""

msgid "There is no dawn object on ubus: either dawn was not built into the firmware, or the service is not running. Enable and start it under \"Mesh networking → Steering (DAWN)\"."
msgstr ""

msgid "This configuration is carried to the peer together with /etc/config/wireless by \"Wired sync\", so both devices score identically; when the peer runs older firmware this step is skipped automatically. After SAVE, DAWN restarts once: an in-flight AP-change decision is interrupted but clients do not drop."
msgstr ""

msgid "This device has a 6 GHz radio, but the current DAWN does not recognise the 6G section"
msgstr ""

msgid "This package declares dawn as a dependency: if this device was built before that dependency was added, install it with opkg install dawn (umdns comes with it) and then reload the page. Until then 802.11k/v/r still work; there is simply nothing to make the \"time to change AP\" decision."
msgstr ""

msgid "To make the score track signal strength exactly (the approach the DAWN docs recommend): set the \"RSSI weight\" of all three bands to 2 and the \"RSSI center\" to -20, and set the good/bad signal scores and the channel-utilization adjustments to 0 for that band. The score then reduces to base score + (RSSI − center) × weight, so even with two APs 20 dB apart the better one wins instead of both falling into the same bucket and scoring the same."
msgstr ""

